-- title:
--   Ogg's unit at a crossing: tt' = p¹²
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p \ge 5$ and a package $\mathfrak X$ of type `DRModelPackage p`, which equips the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the full modular function field at level $p$ over $\mathbb Z$ with properness, flatness and integrality of the structure morphism, normality of its affine sections, curve models over $\mathbb Q$ and over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with their Galois and place compatibilities, two cusp sections over $\mathbb Z$, and a smooth locus. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms `𝔛.compInf κ` and `𝔛.compZero κ`, and let $x_n :=$ `𝔛.crossingPt O κ toκ n` be its image in the base change `baseChangeO p O`, the fibre product of `DRModel.toBase p` with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb Z \to O$, under `pullback.fst` followed by `𝔛.compInf κ` followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`. Assume that the points `𝔛.ξinf O κ toκ` and `𝔛.ξzero O κ toκ` each specialise to $x_n$. Then the stalk of `baseChangeO p O` at $x_n$ contains elements $t, t'$ with $t t' = g^{12}$, where $g$ is the germ at $x_n$ of the global section of the base change obtained from $p \in O$ by pulling back along the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} O$, with $t$ in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and with the image of $t$ a unit under at least one of the two specialisation maps from the stalk at $x_n$ to the stalk at `𝔛.ξinf O κ toκ`, respectively at `𝔛.ξzero O κ toκ`.
--
--   This is the arithmetic input at a crossing point of the geometric $p$-fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model: the germ of Ogg's modular unit $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$ gives a local equation $t$ for one of the two branches through the crossing, with $t t'$ a twelfth power of the uniformiser, and $t$ invertible along the other branch; which branch is left open, so the disjunction absorbs the orientation. It feeds the description of oriented local charts at the crossings, [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart).
